msgid "Warning: there are two different functions B<basename>(); see below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "B<dirname> and B<basename> break a null-terminated pathname string into "
#| "directory and filename components.  In the usual case, B<dirname> returns "
#| "the string up to, but not including, the final '/', and B<basename> "
#| "returns the component following the final '/'.  Trailing '/' characters "
#| "are not counted as part of the pathname."
msgid ""
"The functions B<dirname>()  and B<basename>()  break a null-terminated "
"pathname string into directory and filename components.  In the usual case, "
"B<dirname>()  returns the string up to, but not including, the final \\[aq]/"
"\\[aq], and B<basename>()  returns the component following the final \\[aq]/"
"\\[aq].  Trailing \\[aq]/\\[aq] characters are not counted as part of the "
"pathname."
msgstr ""
"B<dirname> e B<basename> quebram uma sequência de um nome de caminho "
"terminada em NULO em componentes 'diretório' e 'nome de arquivo'. Na forma "
"comum, B<dirname> retorna a sequência até a '/' (exclusive), e B<basename> "
"retorna o componente após a '/' final. Caracteres '/' subseqüentes não são "
"contados como parte do nome do caminho."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "If I<path> does not contain a slash, B<dirname> returns the string \".\" "
#| "while B<basename> returns a copy of I<path>.  If I<path> is the string \"/"
#| "\", then both B<dirname> and B<basename> return the string \"/\".  If "
#| "I<path> is a NULL pointer or points to an empty string, then both "
#| "B<dirname> and B<basename> return the string \".\"."
msgid ""
"If I<path> does not contain a slash, B<dirname>()  returns the string \".\" "
"while B<basename>()  returns a copy of I<path>.  If I<path> is the string \"/"
"\", then both B<dirname>()  and B<basename>()  return the string \"/\".  If "
"I<path> is a null pointer or points to an empty string, then both "
"B<dirname>()  and B<basename>()  return the string \".\"."
msgstr ""
"Se I<path> não contiver uma barra, B<dirname> retorna a sequência \".\", "
"enquanto que B<basename> retorna uma cópia de I<path>. Se I<path> for a "
"sequência \"/\", então tanto B<dirname> como B<basename> retornarão a "
"sequência \"/\". Se I<path> for um ponteiro 'NULO' ou apontar para uma "
"sequência vazia, então tanto B<dirname> como B<basename> retornarão a "
"sequência \".\"."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Concatenating the string returned by B<dirname>(), a \"/\", and the string "
"returned by B<basename>()  yields a complete pathname."
msgstr ""
"A concatenação de uma sequência retornada por B<dirname>(), uma '/', e a "
"sequência retornada por B<basename>() forma um nome de caminho completo."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Both B<dirname>()  and B<basename>()  may modify the contents of I<path>, so "
"it may be desirable to pass a copy when calling one of these functions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"These functions may return pointers to statically allocated memory which may "
"be overwritten by subsequent calls.  Alternatively, they may return a "
"pointer to some part of I<path>, so that the string referred to by I<path> "
"should not be modified or freed until the pointer returned by the function "
"is no longer required."
msgstr ""

